reers in 2016's champions volume 2  number 1 we see part of the aftermath of  the second superhuman civil war already  disillusioned by the actions of her idol  captain marvel her frustration with the  adult superhero community reached its  peak during a mission wanting to be more  proactive in fixing the damage that  their superpowered brawls tend to cause  ms marvel quits the team after captain  america shoots down her suggestion to  fix the train tracks they've just  wrecked she stops her superhero  activities for a few days but eventually  reaches out to nova and spider-man with  an idea a team of newer heroes who will  fix everything their more experienced  peers broke during their dumb war soon  the hulk vibvision and a time traveling  cyclops joined the newly formed  champions under her leadership  the idea of individuals with superpowers  dressing up to fight evil has long been  a sore point in the marvel universe  despite the countless times they've  saved the world and even the universe  with their actions it tends to become an  even bigger problem when the discussion  shifts to the idea of inexperienced  young superheroes with no formal  training the champions especially ms  marvel found themselves at the center of  this issue and 2020s outlawed volume one  number one a standoff at cole's academic  high school involving the super team  renders the stretchy heroine  hospitalized in her civilian identity  and also leads to the passing of an  underage superhero ban in their effort  to protect a climate activist from an  attack by the roxon energy corporation  an unfortunate incident involving viv  vision and the new power man  accidentally causes a building to  collapse while still out of costume  kamala protects the activist with her  body but is rendered comatose this  prompts senator jeffrey patrick to pass  the underage superhuman welfare act  which was named kamala's law to honor  her the champions resist choosing to  fight for their right to operate as  superheroes eventually kamala's law is  repealed and the true villains revealed  thanks to their efforts  kamala khan is typically hailed as a  groundbreaking superhero in the media as  the first muslim character in marvel  comics to star in a self-titled book  however researchers at the london school  of economics and political sciences  middle east center have raised some  valid questions is ms marvel truly  assigned a positive social change or  simply a marketing stunt more  importantly does the character have any  real cross-cultural impact on how the  public perceives identity and talking to  participants from beirut london and  singapore the authors found that  marvel's move to greater diversity with  the introduction of kamala khan was  generally interpreted in two ways some  see it as a means of building better  cultural understanding and breaking down  majority minority tensions while others  think that it's nothing more than a  tokenistic gesture by a multi-billion  dollar entertainment company first off i  just want to say  i get it  it's undeniable that the young ms marvel  does to a significant degree represent a  welcome change in the western  entertainment landscape when it comes to  non-stereotypical representation of  different cultures redefine notes the  obvious similarities between kamala and  peter parker with both of them being  portrayed as regular middle class urban  teenagers saving the day in kamala's  case her being a muslim is not used to  define the core of her character nor is  it portrayed as an obstacle that  prevents her from becoming the best  version of herself regardless of  marvel's motives the push towards  diversity is a welcome one  while the formal announcement of kamala  khan becoming a part of the mcu was  certainly pleasant news to her many fans  there's one core aspect of her character  that got changed in her transition from  the page to the screen in the comics  kamala's dormant and human abilities are  unlocked following her exposure to the  terrigen mists she has both stretching  abilities akin to mr fantastics and  size-changing powers like ant-man in  addition she is a shape-shifter with a  limited healing factor on the other hand  her live-action counterpart possesses  thought-based light construct powers  which she discovered after wearing an  old bangle belonging to her family this  is so cool is this not nice  why did the creators of the disney plus  show decide to alter miss marvel's power  set and origin story so drastically in  an interview with decider the show's  head writer stated that in the interest  of efficient storytelling they left out  elements involving the terrigen mists  and the inhumans in favor of giving  kamala a streamlined origin regardless  fans are sure to be excited to see the  character making her way into the mcu  whether she's in beginning or not  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite comic characters are  coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  you
 

